        "Journaling protects file system structure, not unsaved application data: the document you never saved is still gone after a clean recovery. Snapshots are not backups either, since they usually live on the same volume as the data. Incremental restores need the full backup plus every incremental since, in order; skipping one corrupts the set, a trap {S} answers should name.",
