        "Work a full subnet: given 172.20.8.0/22, compute mask 255.255.252.0, the address count 1024, usable hosts 1022, the broadcast 172.20.11.255, and first and last usable hosts 172.20.8.1 and 172.20.11.254. Splitting into /23s yields two subnets of 510 usable hosts each. Confirm the ranges never overlap and that headroom fits the faculty plan. One worked example demonstrates every skill the addressing unit of {S} expects.",
        "Size a transfer: a 40 GB backup over a 100 Mbps dedicated link moves 320,000 megabits, needing 3200 seconds, about 53 minutes, in theory; schedule it overnight with headroom for retransmission. Pair the calculation with a policy line, backups run between 22:00 and 05:00, and the design answer writes itself, the pattern {S} rewards.",
        "Budget a small branch: two managed switches, one router, one firewall, two access points, structured cabling for 25 desks, a UPS, and a 50 Mbps dedicated circuit with 20 Mbps broadband backup. Annual recurring bandwidth plus support typically overtakes hardware cost by year two, which is why designs state both figures separately and plan upgrades rather than improvise them, the budgeting habit {S} builds.",
